now as former chairman of the ERG group  of brexit territory MPS Steve Baker  Will's big influence in those circles  he's now a minister in the Northern  Ireland office and joins us now thank  you very much good morning  I feel like you were one of the few  concert remps who has been quite  difficult to predict who are you going  to back in this race and you back to  Boris Johnson back in 2019 at the last  what race you back Liz truss via Zoella  Braverman where's your vote going this  time this time around I'm very proud to  back Rishi sennak and why is that that  he's going to deliver competent capable  professional government that we can rely  on if above all what we need is  stability we need professionalism we  need to move this country forward from a  position of great difficulty and rishi's  the right guy to do it last time you  know you supported solo Braverman you  then switch your vote to Liz truss I  mean it felt a little bit like that's  kind of anyone but Rishi so what's  changed no that's not the case so when  we got down to Rishi versus Liz I felt  we had two fantastic candidates to offer  to the membership I was backing Liz  because that was the choice which Sue  Ella and the Euro Skeptics made I was  proud to backliz but realistically if  you look at the summer I didn't campaign  very hard and that was because I was  very happy with either candidate and the  truth is that it was quite a marginal  decision for me and I'm very proud to  back Rishi this time okay now everyone  is talking about Boris Johnson it feels  like he is perhaps the biggest threat to  Rishi student right now when you're  flying back from his Caribbean uh  holiday will you wait or won't you run  looked in late night talks with Rishi  sunak do you think he would be a good  prime minister second time around  there's a lot of love out there for  Boris Johnson and I respect that I mean  I've been a big fan of Boris Johnson so  many times but this isn't the time for  boris's style I mean I'm afraid the  trouble is because of the Privileges  vote Boris would be a guaranteed  disaster there's going to be a vote  before the House of Commons on this  issue of privileges whether he worked  deliberately misled the house in that  though it's guaranteed there'll be a  large number of conservatives who will  refuse as they see it to lay down their  integrity to save him and at that moment  his Premiership will collapse now the  best argument I've heard for dealing  with that is having the vote on the  first day but that relies on people  believing that other MPS think like they  do that you don't vote against a new  prime minister that isn't what will  happen 62 MPS resigned from his his  government over the pincher Affair which  in the end whatever one thinks about it  was an issue of conduct and character  well those same MPS are not now going to  go like Lambs through the division Lobby  so at that moment that there's a vote in  the House of Commons on privilege his  Premiership would collapse it's a  guaranteed nailed on failure and we  cannot allow it to happen so you think  that a sizable number of conservative  MPS would actually vote to say that he  misled one Member of Parliament rang me  on Friday to say that they would rather  lose the whip than vote for Boris  Johnson in that vote and there's why  because they think they're going to lose  their seats and they'll need to make a  living and in order to make a living  they'll need their reputations and this  is why they'd rather lose the whip than  vote for Boris in that division so I'm  sorry voters out there love him and he's  undoubtedly a wonderful man he lights  the room up when he's in the room but  unfortunately he doesn't have that you  know meticulous compliance with tedious  rules he just doesn't do it and it's  caught up with him and and I'm afraid  whatever people would like to be true we  need to just ruthlessly face the truth  as it is and the truth as it is is when  that vote comes which it will his  Premiership would implode and this  country cannot be afford to be back here  in a couple of months how would you vote  in that vote well it depends what  exactly what the vote is but I'm  committed that whoever wins this contest  I will give them absolutely all the  support I can because it's in the  National interest to do so but equally  I'm not  I'm not willing to lay down my Integrity  for Boris Johnson I'm not and um we'll  just have to see what any vote is but  really I want Rishi to win and I want  conservative members to please engage  with this reality and I know people  don't  people love Boris and there'll be people  out there leaping to social media to  call me all sorts of names under the Sun  but that's not important to me what's  important is how this country works out  and fairs if Boris is in charge his  Premiership will implode and we'll be  back here and I know look we haven't  seen the details of the vote the  privilege committee you know they  haven't done their report yet but you  can't rule out voting against him then  you I can't rule it out no but look the  truth is the details aren't really  important this isn't actually a legal  court case this is about the politics of  whether or not people think that Boris  Johnson said or when Boris Johnson said  all the rules had been complied with and  Etc whether he worked knew that actually  they hadn't been and the trouble is  there's so much evidence out there I  think the public have made their minds  up and apart from anything else it's  just too easy for his opponents the  labor party the SNP to absolutely make  hay over this and in those when in those  circumstances when everybody's inboxes  are filling up when the evidence can be  seen by everyone it's just inconceivable  that those members of parliament will  support Boris now his supporters at  Boris Johnson supporters say look he is  the guy with the Mandate he won that  election in 2019 he won all of those  seats many of them who had never voted  for the conservatives before  you've already asked the public to  swallow one unelected prime minister can  you really do the same with another I  really wish we weren't in these  circumstances I really wish we weren't  Liz truss made a mistake she went too  hard and fast she said that she's  apologized I really regret it I could  not have foreseen this would happen but  what I can now foresee is that the best  person to be prime minister of the UK is  Rishi sunak I wish we weren't in these  circumstances but it's Rishi and I I  think that he will accept that the only  set of policies we can carry through are  the ones in the manifesto and I would  expect that Rishi will choose to use  that mandate to press forward the public  don't like elections and the idea that  we should go straight into election now  really is for the birds we need to give  stability to the market sort out the  public finances post this debacle and  move on do you think Boris Johnson  should pull out of the race then I think  it would be technically in I suppose but  yeah I think it would be for the best if  Boris did something big and  statesmanlike I mean if he wants to come  back as prime minister he would need to  do it after this privileges issue is  settled I think he'd make an amazing  chairman of the party everybody knows  he's got huge character Charisma he  lights up any room he's in make him  chairman of the party he can leave the  campaign he confront this government but  he can't be what we can't do is have him  in as prime minister in circumstances  where he's bound to implode taking down  the whole government with him and we  just can't do that again we know of  course that Boris Johnson and Richie  soon like hell talks last night so far  everyone's been very tight-lipped about  what those talks actually were about I  don't suppose you've got any  intelligence for us I haven't though so  that would obviously be very big news  and at the moment until I've come on  your program I'm not on the campaign so  you know I haven't been briefed but I  have spoken to Rishi several times and  I'm confident he'll want to make sure he  really does unite the party and that's  why for example Simon [ __ ] and I on the  other end of the spectrum on brexit he  and I have written an article should be  out as we're speaking saying that we're  coming together behind Rishi and that we  both agree that the current policy on  the Northern Ireland protocol must be  continued and I think this is another  absolutely crucial Point whoever wins  this contest the only policy that can be  successfully carried through on Northern  Ireland is the one that we have  and everyone should understand that  because if if say Rishi doesn't or Penny  didn't carry through that policy the  Euro Skeptics would implode the  government there's absolutely no doubt  they've been very quiet but the Euro  Skeptics really care about this issue of  the whole UK leaving the jurisdiction of  European law and again whatever anyone  else may think that my colleagues like  friends like Bill cash and Mark Francois  and John Redwood they are not going to  tolerate any diversion any equivocation  on this point so whether it's Rishi or  Penny or Boris the same policy must be  carried forward on the Northern Ireland  protocol and I'm very pleased that  actually Simon [ __ ] and I have United  around this point quite different  politicians yeah but not that you  Simon's been very generous to me he's  recognized that I have taken some big  hits  in the apology that I gave to try and  change the negotiating Dynamic and the  friendship between us and Ireland and  it's working it's that's great but I  didn't just speak of humility I also  spoke of resolve everyone needs to  understand that the legitimate interest  of unionists is to end the jurisdiction  of EU law in Northern Ireland now that's  the hardest problem we need to solve but  we will not have devolved government in  in Northern Ireland until it's done that  means we won't be celebrating the 25th  anniversary of the Belfast Good Friday  agreement this is big stuff and everyone  involved needs to understand we can  offer both friendship humility we can  make apologies where they're needed but  in the end we've got to end the  jurisdiction of EU law in Northern  Ireland do you have you had any  assurance from Rishi sunak that he is  going to follow through on what you want  to see yes I have I've spoken to him I  think three times in the last 24 hours  and I'm absolutely not concerned that  Rishi will follow through as he said in  public during the summer campaign he  will follow through on the current  policy but again no one should be in  doubt about this if Simon [ __ ] and I  can agree that the current policy needs  to be carried forwards then the EU and I  hope they'll hear me the EU should  understand there's not going to be a  change of policy you say that if he  doesn't then the Euro Skeptics will  effectively you know well yeah and this  is me just observing I mean people  people should look at recent history and  understand that in similar circumstances  the same effect will happen we know what  a Boris Johnson government will be like  we know how members of parliament will  vote if the privilege when when the  Privileges issue comes up and we know  how eurosceptics will will respond if  they feel betrayed over the Northern  Ireland protocol we just know how they  will and if this is not an issue for me  I don't ever want to be any part of any  kind of rebellion ever again I've done  enough of that for seven years I don't  know quite a lot of it but but the point  is what I'm trying to do this morning I  have done a lot I'm afraid but what I'm  trying to reflect on here is that  irrespective of what I think those  eurosceptic colleagues who I know and  love like like brothers and sisters  they were absolutely not tolerate any  Divergence from what we've said we're  going to do and again look at the recent  past again it doesn't matter whether  people like it or not they will do what  they will do and that is they will bring  down any prime minister who doesn't  deliver on this issue now I've got to  ask listross has been the shortest  serving prime minister ever you know  we've had an entire budget jumped yeah  emergency action by the bank of England  to stop Iran on pensions mortgage costs  spiraling yes you know Labor's now  leading by over 30 points in the polls  and you backed her at the last Allegiant  election you've also served you know  four hours a government Minister you  know do you take any personal  responsibility for what we've seen over  the last few months I certainly feel  personally responsible for helping her  become Prime Minister I did some work in  the Parliamentary phase and some work  um in the phase in the country but I  really don't think I can have been  expected to foresee that she would go as  hard and as fast as she did I wanted as  I said earlier I thought they were both  fantastic candidates and I think  actually that Liz and rescue wanted this  at want and wanted the same destination  I mean I have discussed with Rishi  several times the big problem in the  public finances in the long run but um I  wanted Liz Liz's change of Direction but  I'm afraid you when you're trying to  shift a super tanker you can't fly in  like Superman and hit it at Mac 2 you  just go through the sides and punch a  hole and that's what she's done  um so yeah I do accept there is some  responsibility but equally I was not in  the treasury I didn't sit down with her  and quasi and do this budget and I  remember standing there as we all heard  him make his statement and unlike a  normal financial event it was largely  heard in silence because I would think  we all could understand this is spending  too much money and cutting too much tax  so you know I didn't foresee that  happening okay now just to finish this  is something else I have to ask you made  a few headlines this week when Christian  and Guru Murphy uh called you a  four-letter word I definitely can't  repeat on a Sunday morning uh which  they've picked up on a audio feed yeah  at channel 4 news and he's been  disciplined have been taken off air for  a week do you think that's an  appropriate action well it's really a  matter for channel four I've accepted  his apology and for me that's the end of  it and God bless him since it's a Sunday  morning God bless him to be fair to him  I was absolutely tearing strips off him  in a live interview that's because they  told me it was a pre-record down the  line and I felt his questions were poor  once and I was trying to deliberately  give him answers he couldn't use in a  pre-record but unfortunately they put me  live on air when telling me it was a  pre-record and the result was that I was  tearing strips off him live on air so  I'm not surprised that his blood was up  and I forgive him and that's the end of  it okay uh that's very good thank you  very much for being on the program there  at Stevens revealing he's going to be  backing Rishi sunak in the race to be  the next prime minister

